From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:44:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 202/342] media_addon_server: later flavors' nodes without
 asking itself (M45)

The physical nodes of flavors that come later are made in the control
thread, which answers the server's own requests; a global flavor's
BMediaRoster::InstantiateDormantNode() would have sent it one and waited
for itself. They are made as that request's handler makes them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/servers/media_addon/MediaAddonServer.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/servers/media_addon/MediaAddonServer.cpp b/src/servers/media_addon/MediaAddonServer.cpp
index 0b4c53537b..abe92cf937 100644
--- a/src/servers/media_addon/MediaAddonServer.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/media_addon/MediaAddonServer.cpp
@@ -755,8 +755,20 @@ MediaAddonServer::_InstantiatePhysicalInputsAndOutputs(AddOnInfo& info,
 
 			TRACE("MediaAddonServer::InstantiatePhysialInputsAndOutputs: "
 				"\"%s\" is a physical input/output\n", flavorinfo->name);
-			status_t status = fMediaRoster->InstantiateDormantNode(
-				dormantNodeInfo, &node);
+			status_t status;
+			if (onlyNew) {
+				// this runs in the control thread, the one that answers
+				// the add-on server's requests: a global flavor's request
+				// would wait for itself, so it is instantiated here as that
+				// request's handler does
+				status = MediaRosterEx(fMediaRoster)->InstantiateDormantNode(
+					info.id, flavorinfo->internal_id,
+					(flavorinfo->flavor_flags & B_FLAVOR_IS_GLOBAL) != 0
+						? Team() : -1, &node);
+			} else {
+				status = fMediaRoster->InstantiateDormantNode(
+					dormantNodeInfo, &node);
+			}
 			if (status != B_OK) {
 				ERROR("MediaAddonServer::InstantiatePhysialInputsAndOutputs "
 					"Couldn't instantiate node flavor, internal_id %" B_PRId32
